DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy command outputs DS  (Delegation  Signer)  resource
       records (RRs), or CDS (Child DS) RRs with the _-_C option.

       By  default,  only  KSKs are converted (keys with flags = 257).  The _-_A
       option includes ZSKs (flags = 256).  Revoked keys are never included.

       The input keys can be specified in a number of ways:

       By default, ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy reads a  key  file  named  in  the  format
       KKnnnnnnnn..++aaaaaa++iiiiiiiiii..kkeeyy, as generated by _d_n_s_s_e_c_-_k_e_y_g_e_n.

       With  the  _-_f _f_i_l_e option, ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy reads keys from a zone file
       or partial zone file (which can contain just the DNSKEY records).

       With the _-_s option, ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy reads a kkeeyysseett-- file, as generated
       by _d_n_s_s_e_c_-_k_e_y_g_e_n _-_C.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --11     This option is an abbreviation for _-_a _S_H_A_1.

       --22     This option is an abbreviation for _-_a _S_H_A_-_2_5_6.

       --aa aallggoorriitthhmm
              This option specifies a digest algorithm to use when  converting
              DNSKEY  records  to  DS records. This option can be repeated, so
              that multiple DS records are created for each DNSKEY record.

              The algorithm must be one of SHA-1, SHA-256, or  SHA-384.  These
              values  are  case-insensitive, and the hyphen may be omitted. If
              no algorithm is specified, the default is SHA-256.

       --AA     This option indicates that ZSKs are to be included when generat‐
              ing DS records. Without this option, only keys  which  have  the
              KSK  flag  set are converted to DS records and printed. This op‐
              tion is only useful in _-_f zone file mode.

       --cc ccllaassss
              This option specifies the DNS class; the default is IN. This op‐
              tion is only useful in _-_s keyset or _-_f zone file mode.

       --CC     This option generates CDS records rather than DS records.

       --ff ffiillee
              This option sets zone file mode, in which the final dnsname  ar‐
              gument  of  ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy  is  the  DNS domain name of a zone
              whose master file can be read from ffiillee. If the zone name is the
              same as ffiillee, then it may be omitted.

              If ffiillee is --, then the zone data is read from the  standard  in‐
              put. This makes it possible to use the output of the _d_i_g command
              as input, as in:

              ddiigg ddnnsskkeeyy eexxaammppllee..ccoomm || ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy --ff -- eexxaammppllee..ccoomm

       --hh     This option prints usage information.

       --KK ddiirreeccttoorryy
              This  option tells BIND 9 to look for key files or kkeeyysseett-- files
              in ddiirreeccttoorryy.

       --ss     This option enables keyset mode, in which the final dnsname  ar‐
              gument  from ddnnsssseecc--ddssffrroommkkeeyy is the DNS domain name used to lo‐
